39
00:01:50,680 --> 00:02:13,260
Don't forget to show up.

40
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:20,180
It's Garenu. Sorry for the wait.

41
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:21,320
What's going on?

42
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:26,200
It's been almost 240 hours since Team Titsgera left, right?

43
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:27,040
Yeah.

44
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:30,320
I can tell you right now they won't be returning.

45
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:31,520
Why not?

46
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:35,020
Gintryu's team has started camping out at the start point.

47
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:40,480
We decided beforehand that they wouldn't return to the game until I sent them in all clear.

48
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,900
It was something of a safety precaution.

49
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:47,060
Understood. But their card data will disappear, right?

50
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,380
I'm holding on to all the cards of value.

51
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:52,700
Doesn't that just make it obvious that they have allies?

52
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:55,580
They'll notice none of the four have anything important.

53
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:03,920
They left the game at 3.05 ten days ago. Isn't that right?

54
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:09,760
Yeah. Only five more minutes till their card data is completely wiped. They basically quit.

55
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:12,980
We'll wait until 3.10 just to be safe.

56
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:17,240
All right. But do you really think they've given up?

57
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:21,580
Absolutely. Why else would they take off with Batera and run?

58
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:25,700
It looks like it was just a desperate attempt to keep us from getting the reward money.

59
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:30,200
Maybe you're right. But those guys have spent years collecting those 96 cards.

60
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:34,800
Besides, why would Batera call off his guards? It doesn't make any sense to me.

61
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:37,660
Yeah, but so what? Something probably happened.

62
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:40,940
Well, there's no point in speculating about it now.

63
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:45,720
Oh, look. 3.10 already. Time's up, I guess.

64
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:48,860
Yeah! Bye-bye, Tezgera!

65
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:50,900
Fake?

66
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:57,960
That's right. We switched several of their cards with fake ones. About 30 of the total 96 of them they have.

67
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:06,020
I'm actually holding the 96. For such a cautious guy, this is the biggest gamble of Tezgera's life.

68
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:13,360
So, I just want to make sure it pays off. And I'm really sorry, but I'm not going to be able to help you guys face Team Genthru.

69
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,460
No problem. But when do you want us to give you the card?

70
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:21,820
We can wait until you've defeated Genthru. Good luck, okay?

71
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:32,140
Now we'll go after those brats. It wasn't in the plan, but we can get Strip of Beach from them without too much trouble.

72
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:34,980
But first, we need more copies of a company.

73
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:35,900
Okay.

74
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:40,960
They're on the move! Hey, where are you guys right now?

75
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:42,280
Near Soframi.

76
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:48,240
Looks like they're all heading to Masadora. And as soon as they've got everything ready, I'm sure they'll be coming for you.

77
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:49,340
Are you ready?

78
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:52,880
All set here. You've all been a big help, thanks.

79
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:58,880
We need more time, but we have no choice. It's up to Gon now.

80
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:04,640
Gon! Did you let our conversation distract you from your current objective?

81
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,720
Just tell me what this is about.

82
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:18,040
I hope you'll forgive me, but I took the liberty of picking this up.

83
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:24,040
Is this your daughter? Or granddaughter, perhaps?

84
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:28,540
She was my lover.

85
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:32,640
She'd been in the hospital.

86
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:36,220
She'd been comatose for some time.

87
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:41,220
A few days ago, she passed away in her sleep.

88
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:52,200
I suppose it was because she didn't want people to think she was only after my money, but she returned every expensive gift I gave her.

89
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:55,560
Every single one.

90
00:05:55,560 --> 00:06:00,260
But she loved this picture frame I clumsily made myself.

91
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:10,740
All we ever needed was each other, and we swore that we would never be apart.

92
00:06:10,740 --> 00:06:20,700
Until the accident, when she fell into a deep sleep, never to awaken again.

93
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:32,080
Honestly, she just looked like she was only sleeping.

94
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:39,580
And it was then that I first heard about Greed Island.

95
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:46,980
And if I could only beat that game, I could obtain the one item I needed most.

96
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:49,180
It was like a dream come true.

97
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:56,560
I was fully prepared to spend my entire fortune on copies of that game.

98
00:06:56,560 --> 00:07:01,960
But now, it's all over.

99
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:05,380
It doesn't matter anymore.

100
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:13,600
The Brats have four copies of a company.

101
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:17,180
We have six ourselves. Ready?

102
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,820
Hell yeah! You just say the word.

103
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:22,880
I'll take the kid who has the spiky black hair.

104
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:26,700
Assuming that we have to resort to force, that is.

105
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:28,700
Sub, take the cat-eyed one.

106
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,240
Bara, the girl.

107
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:33,460
Accompany on! Goon!

108
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:38,700
What do you want?

109
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:40,480
No need to be hostile.

110
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:42,320
Let's just make a deal.

111
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,900
With you? We're not interested.

112
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:49,680
Right. Don't let them notice we've been waiting for them.

113
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:52,140
They can't know we're fully prepared.

114
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,980
It's not a bad deal, you know.

115
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:58,180
In fact, it's so good that even Tezgera agreed to it.

116
00:07:58,640 --> 00:07:59,380
What is it?

117
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:00,560
Curious now?

118
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:03,180
Don't move! You can talk from over there!

119
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:06,200
Yes. Very good.

120
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:09,400
We have to make it seem like we're weak and at a disadvantage.

121
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:14,940
We must try to create the impression that we only just arrived here

122
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:16,840
after being cornered in a chase.

123
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:19,480
It's actually surprisingly simple.

124
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:22,640
We'll beat the game on everyone's behalf.

125
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:26,700
Then everyone returns to the real world and splits Patera's reward.

126
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:29,080
I find that hard to believe.

127
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:31,520
We've had a little change of heart.

128
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:34,700
And Tezgera and the others have already left the game.

129
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:35,420
Yeah.

130
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:38,220
But that still doesn't prove that he agreed to your offer.

131
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:39,840
Yes, that's true.

132
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:43,300
Then you'd rather die here?

133
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:47,480
Just shut up and give us all your cards!

134
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,900
Otherwise, we'll kill all of you!

135
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,600
Finally showing your true colors, huh?

136
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:53,500
Look!

137
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:54,780
Company on!

138
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:55,980
To Sofrabi!

139
00:08:58,980 --> 00:08:59,240
Hmm.

140
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:01,140
Three more times.

141
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:06,240
Two more times.

142
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:11,600
Only one more time.

143
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,240
Return on!

144
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,360
Masadora!

145
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:18,760
Masadora?

146
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:21,400
Are they trying to obtain more spell cards?

147
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:24,440
They might try to reach the real world through the harbor.

148
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:26,440
Accompany on!

149
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:26,840
Go!

150
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:31,300
They're not here.

151
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:33,340
Are they concealing their presence?

152
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:34,980
Check the store.

153
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:37,940
Don't want them getting their hands on any spell cards.

154
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:41,240
They haven't been here.

155
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:43,500
Maybe they took off for the harbor.

156
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,520
We have no choice.

157
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:47,820
Accompany on!

158
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:48,400
Go!

159
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:54,780
Don't lose sight of them!

160
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,960
We're completely out of accompanies!

161
00:09:56,960 --> 00:10:08,920
Now, why don't you give up and hand over your cards?

162
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:10,900
You're crazy!

163
00:10:11,220 --> 00:10:12,640
We'll never let you have them!

164
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:15,580
Everything is going as planned.

165
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:17,800
They want to fight us one-on-one.

166
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:21,140
If you want our cards, come and get them!

167
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:21,960
Wait, what?

168
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:23,360
Damn it!

169
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,000
Nice.

170
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:27,840
Now we just need to separate them little by little.

171
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:29,220
Bisky!

172
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:30,820
Get out of here now!

173
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:31,960
I-I...

174
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,180
I said run!

175
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:34,540
Stop!

176
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:37,240
You're not getting away!

177
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:39,220
I'm counting on you two.

178
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:43,640
Sorry, kid, but you're all mine now!

179
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:59,040
I-I...

180
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:02,480
So tell me...

181
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,980
You do know that I'm the bomber, don't you?

182
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,700
I heard it from Tezgyera!

183
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:08,900
Oh?

184
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:14,100
I see. And who told you how my ability works then?

185
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:22,000
Incredible. All it took was that one moment, and he figured out exactly why I'm so wary.

186
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:26,320
And why. That can only come from battle experience.

187
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:33,100
Not too many people know of my ability. And even fewer who have survived long enough to tell anyone.

188
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:34,420
Fuck!

189
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,380
I can't let him take control.

190
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:45,020
Look, I really hate the idea of taking cards from other people by force. So promise me right now!

191
00:11:45,660 --> 00:11:50,020
Whichever of us surrenders first has to give up all his cards to the winner, okay?

192
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:55,840
I think you might have the wrong idea. You're in no position to be making demands.

193
00:11:56,360 --> 00:12:00,800
I'm not gonna bend on this one. Without a promise, this is highway robbery.

194
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:07,560
I'd rather die than give my cards to a thief. Kill me if you want to. I won't open my binder again!

195
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:13,000
You're a real lunatic. But not the same kind of crazy like me.

196
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:16,660
All right. I promise then. And book!

197
00:12:16,660 --> 00:12:23,040
I'm holding 131 cards. 97 are specified slot cards.

198
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:29,120
I have 102. As for specified slots, I've got 71. And book!

199
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:32,780
You have 2 and 75, right?

200
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:33,540
Yeah!

201
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:34,920
Book!

202
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,300
That's all I need.

203
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:38,300
That's all I need.

204
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,040
Good Wren.

205
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:50,040
But it's clear he still has a long way to go.

206
00:12:50,040 --> 00:13:02,080
The best defense is a strong offense. And besides, a single explosion won't be enough to finish you off.

207
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:05,000
So stay on the attack!

208
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:15,540
This kid has skill. But his use of Aura is sloppy at best.

209
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:20,060
I can't imagine why he was so confident.

210
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:27,440
You're not on his level at this point. You won't be able to do much damage.

211
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:30,200
But keep attacking anyway!

212
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:36,320
You will get hurt!

213
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:42,020
You still haven't answered my question.

214
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:44,640
Who told you about my ability?

215
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:48,480
Well, it's not important.

216
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:50,600
What I want to say is

217
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:54,160
that I don't need to use my ability to deal with you.

218
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:59,180
Exactly as planned.

219
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,240
Once he's seen how much stronger he is,

220
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,560
we'll reel him in

221
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:05,280
and spring the trap.

222
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:06,800
Us!

223
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,220
That's how I'd like to respond.

224
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:13,760
But I don't want to be on the losing end forever!

225
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:17,880
I'll make him use his power

226
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,880
and finish the plan later!

227
00:14:20,820 --> 00:14:21,040
Hmm.

228
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:24,060
Looking to get hurt some more?

229
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:44,280
Use your ability!

230
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,500
Cause I've got a surprise for you!

231
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:48,460
I know what you're thinking.

232
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:51,240
And I won't use it!

233
00:14:51,240 --> 00:15:01,540
Damn brat!

234
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:09,700
She's a lot faster than I thought.

235
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:11,540
Fuck!

236
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:15,100
She should be all out of transport spells.

237
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:17,460
What's she doing?

238
00:15:18,780 --> 00:15:21,700
She used transform to disguise it as another card?

239
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,600
Accompany on!

240
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:24,720
Toso Frohby!

241
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,480
Accompany?

242
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:27,180
Why?

243
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:27,220
Why?

244
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:37,500
I don't get it.

245
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:41,220
Why did you go to all that trouble just for this?

246
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:43,840
Did you want to be alone with me or what?

247
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:45,420
Oh no.

248
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:47,000
It's quite simple, really.

249
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:49,820
I didn't want you begging your little friends for help.

250
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:50,460
Huh?

251
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:52,780
What the hell are you talking about?

252
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:53,800
Idiot.

253
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:57,320
What I'm saying is that I'm stronger than you.

254
00:15:57,320 --> 00:16:06,800
Why you little...

255
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,320
Why you little...

256
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:07,840
Why you little...

257
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:10,700
Why you little...

258
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:15,620
Why you little...

259
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:21,820
So you call those attacks, huh?

260
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:24,620
Well, too bad, because you still can't beat me!

261
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:31,260
I won't go easy on you.

262
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:32,880
It's nothing personal.

263
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,840
That's exactly what I was going to say.

264
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,160
Huh? What?

265
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:41,880
I always let people get a hit in.

266
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:43,120
Like a tribute.

267
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:45,100
Because once I turn back,

268
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:47,980
I have a hard time restraining myself.

269
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:53,440
So I end up killing my opponents!

270
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:04,300
Oh, are you still alive?

271
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:05,760
I'm impressed.

272
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,200
Why would you...

273
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:10,360
hide your power if...

274
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,900
you're that strong?

275
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:13,300
Two reasons.

276
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:15,860
First, never show your hand.

277
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:19,640
And second, I absolutely despise my appearance!

278
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:22,180
I'm too buff and I hate it!

279
00:17:22,940 --> 00:17:24,980
So do you agree or don't you?

280
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:26,100
Huh?

281
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,180
Guess he passed out.

282
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:40,700
I've got a slight edge in martial arts skill and physical strength,

283
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:42,720
but he has me beat in aura capacity.

284
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:47,060
So I probably won't be able to hurt him with any normal attack.

285
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:50,260
That makes him perfect to experiment on.

286
00:17:50,260 --> 00:17:55,520
Damn it!

287
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:57,900
That hit just felt like a knife in my brain!

288
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:01,060
I can't afford to mess around with this guy.

289
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:10,360
Wrong!

290
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:12,480
Experiment number one!

291
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:15,140
Lightning palm!

292
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:21,380
That wasn't enough to knock him out.

293
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:23,840
But at least I can stun him for a few seconds.

294
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:26,540
Okay.

295
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,420
Experiment number two!

296
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:30,740
A yo-yo?

297
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:36,420
Let's go!

298
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,120
What is he up to?

299
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:43,460
Gah!

300
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:46,600
What the hell?

301
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:47,880
What's it made of?

302
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,040
It's my brother's alloy.

303
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:53,600
He came up with it himself.

304
00:18:54,380 --> 00:18:55,820
Weighs around 50 kilograms.

305
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:57,680
That's a real punch.

306
00:18:58,060 --> 00:18:58,360
See?

307
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:58,860
Gah!

308
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:03,020
Gah!

309
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:11,260
Between the weight and centrifugal force,

310
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:12,420
that really stings.

311
00:19:12,420 --> 00:19:17,720
He's got a habit of leaving his right flank exposed

312
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:19,060
when I attack a certain way.

313
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:21,900
If I could take his yo-yo

314
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:23,440
and leave him empty-handed,

315
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:27,780
he's bound to make the same mistake.

316
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:31,560
Gotcha!

317
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:34,560
Right there!

318
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:39,360
All right!

319
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,060
Time to crush your ribs!

320
00:19:42,740 --> 00:19:43,200
Gah!

321
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:45,600
Uh-oh.

322
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:48,700
Did I forget to mention I have two yo-yos?

323
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:49,320
No.

324
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:49,700
Ugh.

325
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:50,280
Ugh.

326
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:50,700
Ugh.

327
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:50,780
Ugh.

328
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:51,280
Ugh.

329
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:51,780
Ugh.

330
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:52,280
Ugh.

331
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:52,780
Ugh.

332
00:19:52,780 --> 00:19:53,280
Ugh.

333
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:53,380
Ugh.

334
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:53,780
Ugh.

335
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:54,780
Wow.

336
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:56,080
You're still conscious?

337
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:56,740
Ugh.

338
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:57,860
Hey, old man.

339
00:19:57,860 --> 00:20:01,160
Did you know that when you kick me, you raise up your guard arm?

340
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:03,540
It's like you're making your own blind spot.

341
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:04,180
Ugh.

342
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:04,800
Ugh.

343
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:05,380
Wait.

344
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:09,220
He used my blind spot to pull out another yo-yo and attack?

345
00:20:09,220 --> 00:20:11,060
Hang on.

346
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:13,400
So that means that your blocking habit was-

347
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:16,400
Was a fake to make you kick me with your left leg.

348
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:19,400
And when you released your first yo-yo?

349
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,400
Yeah.

350
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:22,400
I knew you picked something up to throw at me.

351
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:26,240
Why'd you use a company to draw me away?

352
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:30,080
To make you focus on a one-on-one fight and dismiss your surroundings.

353
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:32,240
I just don't believe it.

354
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:36,440
In that brief exchange, you had enough time to set three traps?

355
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,620
Three, huh?

356
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:40,320
You gotta be kidding me.

357
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:43,900
Every move I made was a trap.

358
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:50,120
Experiment complete.

359
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:53,040
Looks like they both work.

360
00:20:53,040 --> 00:20:57,620
It's over.

361
00:20:57,620 --> 00:20:59,880
Why don't you accept it?

362
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:01,900
You will never defeat me.

363
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:03,120
Shut up.

364
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:09,120
Shut up! I'm not... finished with you yet!

365
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:14,120
It seems I was wrong.

366
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:19,120
I take back what I said before. You are tough.

367
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:26,120
This is my ability. I'll show it to you.

368
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:39,120
This battle isn't only about the physical. I'm going to crush his spirit. His will to fight, to stand, and to resist.

369
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:43,120
Otherwise, he'll never admit defeat.

370
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:54,120
If I truly want to win, I can't be stubborn. I'll make him see. I'll prove to him that all his hard work and confidence mean absolutely nothing!

371
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,120
Here he comes!

372
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:07,120
The villain has unleashed his true power. Will Gon be able to emerge victorious?

373
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:08,120
wretched....

374
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:14,120
僕らにどんな世界が? 道なき道の先に待ってる?

375
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:21,120
声泣き声はこのまま どこにも届かずに消えてゆくの?

376
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:42,120
忘れない 昨日の日は消せない 今日の後悔も投げ捨て カムシェアに明日を目指す 朝日に照らされた傷 笑い合って 終わることない旅を続けよう

377
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:59,200
向かい風としていながら それでも進む理由がある だから友よ 置いてくためだけに生きるのはまだ 早いだろ

378
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:17,200
身につけたもの 抱え込んだもの 手放したとき 始まる何か 上手く生きてく レシピを破り捨てて 感じるリズム そう僕らのやり方で

379
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:59,180
ご視聴ありがとうございました

